# File store and documents

This run has a file store outside the working directory. It is not a path in bash; the only way
to put something there is the tool `document_write`.

- Create one subdirectory per topic: `<topic>/<file>` as `storePath`.
- Put documents, reports and temporary products there - NOT into the working directory, unless
  they are part of the actual assignment.
- `document_write` takes either the full `content` you wrote or, for an existing file, its
  `file_path` as `read` names it; the server copies that file unchanged, so never retype it.
- The user sees these files in the "Documents" area of the interface, grouped by subdirectory.
- When you spawn agents, name in their task the store path they are supposed to write to.

If the user wants to see the content of a file or a document, show it COMPLETELY via
`show_document` (title = file name or document name) - never paraphrase or shorten. Name an
existing file instead of retyping it: `file_path` for any file `read` reaches (relative to the
working directory, absolute, or with an alias such as `@actors`), `storePath` for a file of the
file store. Only text you produced yourself goes in as `content`.
